(ned LOAD SPINDLE -- PURE drawbar clamp, zero bookkeeping)
; operator 2026-08-04: "loading is just physical action... load is pull
; drawbar back in. no impact to the table whatsoever". The record stays
; whatever it was (normally T0 after an unload); clamping an actual tool
; therefore raises UNRECORDED about 1 s later and the motion lock holds
; until the operator declares it in the tool table (LOC column). That is
; the designed flow, not an error.
o<load_spindle_clamp> sub
M66 P2 L0
o1 if [#5399 EQ 0]
    (ABORT, load_spindle_clamp: shaft not stopped -- not clamping)
o1 endif
o<clamptool> call
o<load_spindle_clamp> endsub
M2
